8
00:01:32,808 --> 00:01:42,528
ALEX: Darden beat earnings but Olive Garden same-store sales growth fell short. Casual dining is finally hitting the wall—consumers are trading down from breadsticks and unlimited soup to whatever costs less.

9
00:01:42,528 --> 00:01:50,053
JAMIE: So the same people who were fine-dining six months ago are now deciding that maybe they don't need the salad course after all.

10
00:01:50,053 --> 00:02:10,746
ALEX: The consumer's out of money. Darden's fine-dining portfolio is still holding up because people with real wealth aren't eating less—but Olive Garden's traffic is slowing because that's where the middle market goes when the credit card bill shows up. When Olive Garden's growth rate drops, it's not noise. It's the canary in the coal mine, except the canary just ordered water instead of a drink.

11
